          }
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "article-metadata",
        "type": "article-metadata"
      },
      {
        "id": "workday-water-intro",
        "type": "content-section",
        "content": {
          "width": "narrow",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Days filled with meetings, messages and deadlines can pass with very few breaks. While concentrating on work, it is easy to overlook small needs that recur throughout the day. Keeping water nearby and using a few simple reminders can make regular fluid intake feel more natural."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": 2,
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Do not wait for the perfect moment"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Instead of turning hydration into another task, connect it with things you already do. Fill a glass before starting work, take a short break between meetings or refill your water with lunch."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "workday-water-photo",
        "type": "article-image",
        "content": {
          "src": "/blog/natural-origin.webp",
          "alt": "A glass of water on a tidy desk",
          "width": 1600,
          "height": 1000,
          "caption": "Keeping water within reach can be a simple reminder during a busy workday.",
          "layout": "medium"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "workday-water-actions",
        "type": "content-section",
        "content": {
          "width": "narrow",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": 2,
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Three practical steps"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": true,
              "items": [
                [
                  {
                    "text": "Prepare drinking water at your workspace before you begin."
                  }
                ],
                [
                  {
                    "text": "Use a change of task as a moment to check whether you feel thirsty."
                  }
                ],
                [
                  {
                    "text": "Adjust your water intake to activity, temperature and personal needs."
                  }
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "There is no need to follow one fixed number of glasses each day. Water needs vary, and we also get fluids through food and other drinks."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": 2,
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Breaks have another purpose too"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "A short break from your screen can be a chance to stand, stretch and change position. A glass of water does not solve every problem related to prolonged sitting, but it can be one small part of a better-organized workday."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "workday-water-end",
        "type": "content-section",
        "content": {
          "width": "narrow",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": 2,
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Consistency matters more than perfection"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "The best routine is one that you can maintain. Simple habits adapted to real responsibilities are often more useful than ambitious rules quickly abandoned."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
